## EPICs 004/005/006 — Advertising Amazon (Business Q&A)

**Status:** Q&A session active — Diana Takach joined via Teams DM (2026-04-16 ~18:46 UTC)
**Sections Q1.1–Q1.5: ✅ DECIDED**
**Answers captured so far:**
- ACoS: Calculate breakeven ACoS → apply down-multiplier. Varies by campaign type & product margin.
- Bids: Amazon bid recommendations = sanity check, not source of truth.
- Campaign structure: Different bids per campaign type → separate distinct campaigns.
- Format decision: New artifact; lowest friction = conversational (option B).
- **Q1.4c (ToS placement premium):** Performance-based — increase by 10% increments when ACOS is strong, evaluate L7.
- **Q1.4d (Brand targeting ROAS floor):** $20+ ROAS typical for brand campaigns. $8 ROAS = floor for scaling. Deferred to Nik for per-product specifics.
- **Q1.5 (Auto-targeting):** Bid highest close-match, moderate substitutes, lower loose-match, lowest/paused complements. Starting bid ratios = editable inputs. Performance override = yes (ACOS-driven). Confirmed by Nik.
- **Q1.6 (Bid floor/ceiling):** ✅ DECIDED — Relative cap = 3x ad group default. No minimum bid for now. No absolute ceiling needed (portfolio/campaign caps suffice).
- **Q1.7 (Scale/batch size):** 🟡 PARTIALLY DECIDED — Daily changed-only bids 2AM-6AM ET (pending Diana confirmation). Weekly full sweep day TBD by Diana.
**Remaining:** Q1.7 (partial)–Q1.11, Q2.1–Q2.3, Q3.1–Q3.6, Q4.1–Q4.5
**Next:** Q1.7 (awaiting Diana confirmation on nightly window + weekly sweep day), then Q1.8+

